    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nAvoid `KeyError` in `ScatterSplitReplacementPass` when dead-code elimination removes unused outputs of the post-scatter split.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Replace or redirect only the Q/K/V outputs that still exist, without disabling the optimization.\n- Extend the existing compiler regression test to cover all outputs, Q only, K only, and Q+K in FP16 and BF16. Numerical parity and scatter-removal assertions remain in place.\n\n## Validation\n\nNative B300 validation with Torch 2.14.0+cu130: the original pass fails 6 of the 8 cases with `KeyError`; the patched pass passes all 8. The two original all-output cases pass in both arms. Both arms use the same tests and normal project fixtures, real `TestBackend`, `RotaryEmbedding`, and Inductor.\n\nReproduce with:\n\n```bash\nuv run --no-project --python .venv/bin/python python -m pytest \\\n  tests/compile/passes/test_scatter_split_replace.py -q\n```\n\nThe native run used a full vLLM `ff01a6b14` package/runtime with the exact pass and test overlaid in separate fresh processes. The original affected files are unchanged through checked main `3788269c98`; this is not a full current-main wheel/build, all-backend, or whole-model qualification. The same 20 dependency/collection warnings occur in both arms. No performance claim.\n\nRuff check/format and typos hooks pass. The repository's test-tethering, SPDX, root-import, forbidden-import, CUDA-call, config, and boolean-context-manager checks also pass. Full pre-commit and mypy remain unverified: Windows application control blocks newly generated hook-environment interpreters during setup. No protection was disabled. Official CI is still needed.\n\n## Details\n\nThe pass builds `split_getitem_users` from the split's surviving users, but previously indexed keys 0, 1, and 2 unconditionally. Guarding each corresponding replacement handles unused outputs while preserving the original rewrite for live outputs. This does not change RoPE math, kernels, configuration, or the pass's matching conditions; it does not claim to handle every partial RoPE graph.\n\nDuplicate checks found no matching open fix (`\"scatter_split\"`, open scatter titles, and open split/KeyError searches). Related #58838 ports RoPE to IR and does not modify this pass or its test; #57299 is already merged and does not contain this guard.\n\nAI assistance was used. The human submitter reviewed the complete two-file diff and the validation results.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
